to start over today, imagine you didn't

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:20.200
have any audience, what would be the

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:23.200
step-by-step playbook to launch a SaaS

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:25.400
in 2026? So, where I would start,

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.800
obviously, is building a personal brand

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.520
on LinkedIn. And it doesn't have to be

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:30.720
the most viral. You don't have to be an

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:32.280
expert. You just have to be useful. So,

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.880
if you're a beginner that wants to start

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:35.320
posting on LinkedIn, the thing that you

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.920
need to understand is what is your

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:38.840
unfair advantage and what can you

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:41.320
educate people on, right? Your unfair

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:43.400
advantages could be your story or the

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.800
tactical subject that you have expertise

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:48.080
on. You can actually create educational

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:49.840
content just about that. And that would

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.880
literally give you the following that

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:53.480
you need to then launch something else.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.320
And then, if you're wondering about the

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:56.920
step-by-step playbook on how to build a

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:59.960
personal brand, I have a framework

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:01.800
called the 4321. So, ideally, you want

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:03.640
to post four times a week. That's it.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:05.640
Not five, not six, not seven. Don't

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.520
overwhelm yourself. Focus on the quality

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:08.760
rather than the quantity. Then, three

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.120
content pillars that you need to be

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:13.280
using. So, educational, storytelling,

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.920
and then sales-generating content. This

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:17.760
could be lead magnets. And the second

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:19.360
thing, the two in that 432 is uh the two

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:21.720
types of audiences you want to be

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:23.640
marketing to. You have your ICP, your

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:26.400
ideal client persona, and you have your

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:27.600
IFP. And that is your ideal follower

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:29.560
persona. So, when you're creating

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:32.240
content for these two types of personas,

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:35.160
you can get leads and demand or waitlist

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:37.320
sign-ups, but you also get a community

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:39.440
that pushes you, likes your content,

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:41.640
engages with you every single day, and

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:44.520
eventually, over time, can also buy from

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:46.480
you. So, the last part of the 4321 was

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:49.000
lead magnets. And now, how you build

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:50.800
them is super simple. You literally only

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.720
have to create a Google document

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:54.240
explaining something or a Loom or

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.760
something else that you already have.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:57.320
Maybe it's a part of your process, and

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.200
then you give it out to people for free.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.600
And the only thing that you ask for is

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:03.160
their email. You send them the lead

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:05.360
magnet, they sign up to your email

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.800
newsletter to get that lead magnet, and

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.600
over time, you just nurture them. And

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:10.480
so, while you're building in public,

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:12.680
creating all of this content, you know,

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:15.200
taking hours of your time writing this

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:17.680
amazing content that potentially will go

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:19.839
viral, the way to guarantee your success

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:21.800
is to have that waitlist in the

00:12:19.839 --> 00:12:22.880
background building. So, when you want

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:24.800
to launch something, when you want to

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.200
offer something, you can. Step number

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:30.080
three, which is my favorite, is

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:32.400
webinars. You can do two types of lives,

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:34.200
a LinkedIn Live, or you can do a Zoom

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:35.880
webinar. For launch number one, we just

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:37.640
did one LinkedIn Live, which is

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:40.040
literally on LinkedIn. You're going live

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:41.480
like you would on Instagram or X. You

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:43.360
tell people that you're going to do it.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:44.560
You create a simple post about it just

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.360
highlighting what it is going to be

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:49.839
about. whoever signs up gets a

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:51.920
notification directly on LinkedIn that

00:12:49.839 --> 00:12:53.680
you're going live. All you need is one

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:55.280
topic to educate on for the first 20

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:57.040
minutes. Then, the next 20 minutes is

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:58.720
going to be a walk-through or a demo.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:00.600
And then, the third bit is you're going

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.200
to be pitching the product, sending the

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:04.040
link, tell them where to buy. When

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:05.800
you're able to show up as a human,

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:08.240
people actually connect with you, with

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:10.680
your mannerisms, with how you look, with

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:12.920
where you live, with how you sound. So,

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:14.920
that's what allowed us to literally hit

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:16.760
the 30K in four days. Once you have your

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:18.320
first couple users or even before you

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.760
launch or when you're doing better

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.920
launches like we did ourselves, the

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:24.680
thing that you need to focus on to make

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:27.680
sure that the product is perfect is hop

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:30.280
on calls or DM customers directly to ask

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:33.040
them for direct support. What we did was

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:35.000
we were going on VIP white-glove

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:36.760
onboarding calls where we literally took

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.880
people through the product so they could

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:40.960
use it correctly. Because the reason why

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:42.640
most people stop using software is

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:44.280
because they don't understand it. It's

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:46.400
not because it doesn't work. So, we

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:48.440
tried our best to make sure that every

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:50.440
single one of our customers at the start

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:52.440
was able to use that product correctly

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:54.440
so then they could stay on for longer.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:56.960
They gave us an amazing testimonial, and

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:58.600
then they became Cleo evangelists. But

00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:01.040
also, in the background, we were

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:03.400
recording those calls to make sure that

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:06.040
we spotted patterns in thinking, in

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:08.120
problems, in bugs, in issues that people

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:10.800
were having so we could actually fix

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:12.839
them immediately. So, it was also an

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:14.640
iteration play for us so we could have

00:14:12.839 --> 00:14:16.480
the best product available as fast as

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:18.640
possible. So then, step number five,

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:20.640
what you need to also do is think about

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:22.440
how can you get the most demand as fast

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:24.959
as possible? You build your waitlist,

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:27.720
and then to incentivize customers to

00:14:24.959 --> 00:14:29.400
buy, you offer them a lifetime discount

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:31.240
or something that feels exclusive.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:33.040
You're trying to push someone to buy.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:34.240
And there's many ways to do it. With

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:35.520
psychology, you can do it through

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.839
curiosity, you could do it through

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.680
scarcity, or you could do it through

00:14:36.839 --> 00:14:40.240
FOMO. We tried all of them, but the one

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:42.560
that worked best at the start was

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:45.400
scarcity. We told people we only have

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.959
500 spots available, which made people

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:49.160
want to take action faster. When

00:14:46.959 --> 00:14:50.720
something's available so easily, people

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:52.280
don't want to buy it immediately. So,

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.079
you need to add that incentive for

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:55.880
